                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00042         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror begins. Canonical definitions:
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00043         ; wiki/internal/implementation/routine-catalog.html
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00044         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Inputs: Presentation state, interval timer, input edges, current map, and the selected auxiliary profile
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00045         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Outputs: Updated presentation state and the dispatcher retain/release status when applicable
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00046         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00047         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Reads: Presentation direct-page state, cold payloads, authored map streams, and input state
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00048         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Writes: Presentation state, mapped BACK pixels, and presentation-owned persistent metadata
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00049         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Side effects: May retain the foreground interval or produce a complete presentation surface
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00050         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile presentation Invariants: Gameplay simulation begins only after release; hidden hydration may prepare initial-stage state and hold it unchanged until release; FRONT publication remains IRQ-owned
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00051         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Inputs: Source and destination identities, bounded count or stream metadata, and any required mapped page
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00052         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Outputs: Copied, decoded, merged, cached, or addressed data plus caller-visible pointer progress
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00053         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Clobbers: A, B, D, X, Y, U, and condition codes unless a narrower source-local header is present
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00054         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Reads: The declared source stream, table, framebuffer rows, or metadata record
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00055         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Writes: Only the declared bounded destination record, cache, row range, or scratch fields
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00056         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Side effects: May temporarily map a required GIME page while moving or decoding data
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00057         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror profile copy Invariants: Counts and destination bounds are honored; any temporary GIME mapping is restored before returning unless the routine contract explicitly states otherwise
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00058         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror contract demo_runtime_tick profile=presentation: Advance the deterministic release-demo route at eligible semantic cells.
                      (rc/demo_runtime.s):00059         ; DOC-002 source-contract mirror ends.
